{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Real.Lemmas"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing.sign_definite_carrier_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing.sign_definite_carrier_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SLeakZeroCrossing.lean#L166-L178","doc":"**Scope-(b) exclusion of any sign-definite carrier.** No continuous,\n*nowhere-zero* function `g` on the anchor interval `[a, b]` can agree with a carrier\nthat changes sign across the anchors (`g a < 0 < g b`): its intermediate zero\ncontradicts nonvanishing. This sharpens `SRigidityPrune`'s \"not anchor-invariant\"\nto \"must cross zero\", excluding every sign-definite form (`exp∘·`, `|·|`,\nsum-of-squares) regardless of magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing.sleak_zero_between_anchors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakZeroCrossing.sleak_zero_between_anchors","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SLeakZeroCrossing.lean#L152-L164","doc":"**Sign-flip ⇒ zero-crossing.** A continuous `S_leak` on the closed anchor\ninterval `[a, b]` with `S_leak a < 0 < S_leak b` vanishes at some `q*` strictly\ninside `(a, b)`. Applied to the c₃ bar-odd residual (with `a` = proton anchor,\n`b` = muon anchor, per the documented signs), this is the substrate `q*` where\n`c₃ = −Vol(4₁)` exactly — the residual is purely bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0}]}